{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.A8PartitionFunctionIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.A8PartitionFunctionIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.partitionCount_eq_fintype_card_partition_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.partitionCount_eq_fintype_card_partition_small","kind":"axiom","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity.lean#L175-L193","doc":"**Bridge to Mathlib's `Nat.Partition` (semantic link).**\n\nThe local `partitionCount n` equals `Fintype.card (Nat.Partition n)`\nfor the five values used in the `a_8` identity.\n\nThis is the standard Hardy–Ramanujan partition-function table:\n`p(1) = 1, p(2) = 2, p(3) = 3, p(4) = 5, p(5) = 7` (OEIS A000041).\n\nAxiomatised pending a uniform Mathlib `decide`-route for\n`Fintype.card (Nat.Partition n)`; the values themselves are standard and\nuncontested (OEIS A000041: `p(1..5) = 1, 2, 3, 5, 7`).  Verified 2026-08-21\nthat `decide` currently **fails** on the Mathlib `Nat.Partition` Fintype\ninstance (`Tactic decide failed`), so this remains a cited external fact\nrather than a discharged lemma; resolution is a one-line `decide` once that\ninstance becomes `Decidable`-friendly at small `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.a_8_eq_partition_sum_ascending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.a_8_eq_partition_sum_ascending","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity.lean#L138-L151","doc":"**Alternative form (ascending degree).**  Re-indexing the sum\nby `k = 5 - n` gives:\n\n  `a_8(X) = Σ_{k=0..4} p(5-k) · X^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.a_8_eq_partition_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.a_8_eq_partition_sum","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity.lean#L112-L136","doc":"**Main identity (closed form).**  The a_8 Habiro coefficient\npolynomial equals the partition-function-weighted sum:\n\n  `a_8(X) = Σ_{n=1..5} p(n) · X^(5-n)`.\n\nCoefficient-by-coefficient match (descending in X-degree):\n  `X^4 ↔ p(1) = 1, X^3 ↔ p(2) = 2, X^2 ↔ p(3) = 3,\n   X^1 ↔ p(4) = 5, X^0 ↔ p(5) = 7`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:a-8-partition-function-identity","label":"prop:a-8-partition-function-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.partitionCount_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.partitionCount_values","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity.lean#L105-L110","doc":"Concrete values of the partition function for `n = 1..5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.a_8_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.a_8_poly","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity.lean#L99-L103","doc":"**The a_8 Habiro coefficient polynomial** (shared exactly by\nproton and neutron in the canonical Habiro-witness convention):\n\n  `a_8(X) = X^4 + 2·X^3 + 3·X^2 + 5·X + 7`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.partitionCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.A8Partition.partitionCount","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity.lean#L84-L97","doc":"The concrete integer partition function values for `n = 1..5`:\n`(p(1), p(2), p(3), p(4), p(5)) = (1, 2, 3, 5, 7)`.\n\nThis is the value table needed for the `a_8` identity; the\nbridge to Mathlib's `Fintype.card (Nat.Partition n)` is given\nby `partitionCount_eq_fintype_card_partition` below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}